Split ESP32-S3 IRAM around the cache-reserved hole to fix SIMPLE_BOOT boot hang

boards/xtensa/esp32s3/common/scripts/flat_memory.ld
boards/xtensa/esp32s3/common/scripts/esp32s3_sections.ld

WHY
---
The SIMPLE_BOOT image dies with IllegalInstruction at the entry point and a
ROM "SHA-256 comparison failed" (the ROM computes the hash over the IRAM
segment it actually placed in RAM, and that RAM differs from the file).

Root cause (proven by a live RAM dump of run90 via esptool dump_mem):
the ESP32-S3 reserves a block of IRAM for the cache controller.  Addresses
in that block read back as all-zero after the ROM copies the IRAM segment,
so the entry code is fetched as zeros -> IllegalInstruction.  The bad block
is NOT 0x40378000-0x4037C000 (the earlier guess).  The live dump showed:

  - vectors  @ 0x40374000 (len 0x400)  -> byte-identical to file   (GOOD)
  - .iram0.text @ 0x4037c000 (len 0xb58c):
        bytes 0x4037c000 .. 0x4037c910  -> ALL ZERO in live RAM    (BAD)
        bytes 0x4037c910 .. 0x4038758c  -> identical to file       (GOOD)
  - the entry point 0x4037c3fc lies INSIDE the zeroed block.

So the cache-reserved block includes the 0x4037C000 region.  The fix is to
place loaded IRAM entirely ABOVE it, at 0x40380000 (which the dump proved is
clean: real code there matched the file exactly).

FIX
---
iram0_0_seg currently spans 0x40374000 -> SRAM_IRAM_END and straddles the
cache-reserved block.  Split it into two hole-free regions:
  iram0_0_seg : org = SRAM_IRAM_ORG (0x40374000), len = 0x4000  (vectors only)
  iram0_1_seg : org = 0x40380000,          len = SRAM_IRAM_END - 0x40380000
and route .iram0.text / .iram0.text_end / .iram0.data / .iram0.bss to
iram0_1_seg.  .iram0.vectors stays in iram0_0_seg (region A) so vecbase and
the reset vector table are untouched.  No loaded IRAM lands in the bad block,
so the ROM copy is no longer corrupted and the entry code is real.

This is the real fix for the boot hang; the debug probes 0003/0004 can be
reverted once a clean boot is confirmed.

diff --git a/boards/xtensa/esp32s3/common/scripts/esp32s3_sections.ld b/boards/xtensa/esp32s3/common/scripts/esp32s3_sections.ld
index 305256c..13bd98b 100644
--- a/boards/xtensa/esp32s3/common/scripts/esp32s3_sections.ld
+++ b/boards/xtensa/esp32s3/common/scripts/esp32s3_sections.ld
@@ -251,7 +251,7 @@ SECTIONS
     . = ALIGN(4) + 16;
 
     _iram_text = ABSOLUTE(.);
-  } >iram0_0_seg
+  } >iram0_1_seg
 
     /* Marks the end of IRAM code segment */
 
@@ -264,7 +264,7 @@ SECTIONS
     . += 16;
     . = ALIGN(256);
     _iram_end = ABSOLUTE(.);
-  } >iram0_0_seg
+  } >iram0_1_seg
 
   .iram0.data :
   {
@@ -272,7 +272,7 @@ SECTIONS
 
     *(.iram.data)
     *(.iram.data.*)
-  } >iram0_0_seg
+  } >iram0_1_seg
 
   .iram0.bss (NOLOAD) :
   {
@@ -283,7 +283,7 @@ SECTIONS
 
     . = ALIGN(4);
     _iram_end = ABSOLUTE(.);
-  } >iram0_0_seg
+  } >iram0_1_seg
 
   .dram0.dummy (NOLOAD) :
   {
diff --git a/boards/xtensa/esp32s3/common/scripts/flat_memory.ld b/boards/xtensa/esp32s3/common/scripts/flat_memory.ld
index ee0e928..0e6e869 100644
--- a/boards/xtensa/esp32s3/common/scripts/flat_memory.ld
+++ b/boards/xtensa/esp32s3/common/scripts/flat_memory.ld
@@ -118,7 +118,14 @@ MEMORY
 
   /* IRAM for CPU */
 
-  iram0_0_seg (RX) :                 org = SRAM_IRAM_ORG, len = SRAM_IRAM_SIZE
+  /* IRAM split around the ESP32-S3 cache-reserved block at 0x4037C000.
+   * Live RAM forensics on run90 proved addresses 0x4037c000..0x4037c910 come
+   * back all-zero after the ROM copy (entry 0x4037c3fc is inside that block),
+   * while 0x40374000 (vectors) and 0x40380000+ are clean.  Route loaded IRAM
+   * to two hole-free regions, skipping the entire 0x4037C000-0x40380000 block.
+   */
+  iram0_0_seg (RX) :                 org = SRAM_IRAM_ORG, len = 0x4000
+  iram0_1_seg (RX) :                 org = 0x40380000, len = SRAM_IRAM_END - 0x40380000
 
   /* Flash mapped instruction data. */
